---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/site.config';
import { formatDate } from '@/utils/date';

const updated = formatDate(new Date(SITE.privacyUpdated));
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data: what’s collected, cookies, advertising and analytics, and your choices.`}
  intro={`Last updated: ${updated}`}
>
  <p>
    This page explains what information is collected when you visit {SITE.name}, how it’s used, and the choices you
    have. We keep it short and in plain language.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    You don’t need an account to use {SITE.name}, and we don’t ask for your name, email or any other personal details
    to read the guides.
  </p>
  <p>
    Like almost every website, our hosting provider automatically records basic technical information when you visit,
    such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you request. This is used to deliver the site, keep it secure
    and fix problems.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We may use an analytics service to understand how many people visit and which guides are most useful. We use this
    information in aggregate only, to improve the site. If we use an analytics service that sets cookies, we’ll name it
    here.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} may show ads to cover its costs. If we do, third-party vendors, including <strong>Google</strong>, may
    use cookies to serve ads based on your previous visits to this and other websites.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google’s use of advertising cookies lets it and its partners serve ads based on your visits to this site and/or
      other sites on the internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can learn more about how Google uses data at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener"
        >How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can also opt out of many third-party vendors’ use of cookies at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can block or delete cookies at any time in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Our guides sometimes link to other websites. We’re not responsible for their content or privacy practices, so
    please check their policies too.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is not directed at children under 13, and we don’t knowingly collect personal information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change how we handle data, we’ll update this page and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  {
    SITE.contactEmail ? (
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? See our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    )
  }
</PageLayout>
